# vvaharness/util/counters.py

Process-wide stage counters: integers that are added to and string notes that are overwritten. Read once by `metrics.build()`, and also read mid-stage by code that compares a counter before and after a call (for example `s8_chain.py` checks whether the ranked-invalid counter moved; `s6_verify.py` reads `s6_confidence_clamped`).

Source: `vvaharness/util/counters.py` (lines 1-88)
Executor: code
Called from: every stage (`COUNTERS.bump`, `COUNTERS.note`), `vvaharness/util/metrics.py` (snapshot), `vvaharness/pipeline/stages/s8_chain.py` and `s6_verify.py` (`COUNTERS.get`)

// src: vvaharness/util/counters.py:22-86
_Counters {
  State { _ints: Map; _notes: Map; _retired_ints: Map; _retired_notes: Map }   // all under one lock

  // src: counters.py:34-41
  fn bump(name, n=1):executor=code {
    require name is not already a note (current or retired) => throw ValueError("a name must be either a count or a note, never both")
    _ints[name] += n
  }
  // src: counters.py:43-51
  fn note(name, value):executor=code {
    require name is not already a count (current or retired) => throw ValueError
    _notes[name] = value   // last writer wins
  }
  fn get(name, default=0) { return _ints[name] or default }   // src: counters.py:53-55
  fn snapshot() { return _ints merged with _notes }            // src: counters.py:57-59
  fn snapshot_cumulative() { return retired plus current counts, then notes }   // src: counters.py:61-67
  // src: counters.py:69-85
  fn reset() { add current ints into retired; copy notes into retired notes; clear current }   // between repositories
  fn reset_all() { clear everything, cumulative history included }
}
COUNTERS = _Counters()   // src: counters.py:88
